  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-24T17:06:14.441Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm trying out the beta version of PhysBone and it's great! Thank you and your staff for making this.\nI used DynamicBone for hair and clothes when making games and movies in Unity.\nSo I was able to almost divert the dynamics of the game models and avatar models.\nHowever, after using PhysBone this time, I wanted to change my main assets from DynamicBone to PhysBone.\nHowever, there was a problem with that: if I imported all the SDKs, it would include the avatar-related stuff, the pipeline manager, and so on.\nI believe PhysBone is in demand on its own.\nWould you consider distributing PhysBone separately from the SDK or selling it in the Unity asset store?\n(I'm not an English speaker, so I use a translation tool. Sorry if this comes across as rude, I'm just trying to be helpful).",
